            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0839" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10101</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bundy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-31T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 31, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 21, 10 a.m. Say to Liberian Government that the Government of the United
                    States, while fully appreciating the apprehension which induced Liberia’s
                    action, would as her best friend desire to point out that Liberia having
                    declared war against Germany, should act in the common interest and recognize
                    that wireless communication with Liberia is necessary not only for the
                    successful operation of the ships of the Associated Governments on the west
                    coast of Africa, but for the very protection of Liberia herself, and that by
                    depriving these Governments of the use of the wireless station at Monrovia in
                    the operation of their vessels, Liberia would seem to be, in fact, furthering
                    the interests of the common enemy which this Government is confident Liberia
                    will not wish to do.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
